Concurrency and cancel-in-progress in GitHub Actions - RunsOn

Used well, it cuts wasted compute on PRs and protects your production deploys from getting killed mid-flight.

concurrency:
  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

For deploys and releases, cancelling an in-progress run is the last thing you want — killing a deploy halfway through can leave production in a broken, half-migrated state.
Never use cancel-in-progress: true on deploy or release jobs.
